{"name":"Plush Velvet","hex":"#7e737d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very extravagant. (Can we add an example for this sense?)","Very expensive, or appearing expensive; opulent, luxurious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A textile fabric with a nap or shag on one side, longer and softer than the nap of velvet.","A plush toy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plush"},{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stuffed toy","blocks":[{"text":"A stuffed toy is a toy with an outer fabric sewn from a textile and stuffed with flexible material. They are known by many names, such as stuffed animals, plush toys, plushies, stuffies and teddies; in Britain and Australia, they may also be called soft toys or cuddly toys. Stuffed toys are made in many different forms, but most resemble real animals, mythological creatures, cartoon characters, or inanimate objects. They can be commercially or home-produced from numerous materials, most commonly pile textiles like plush for the outer material and synthetic fiber for the stuffing. Often designed for children, some stuffed toys have become fads and collector's items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg/330px-Nachbildung_55PB_Steiff_Museum_Giengen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuffed_toy"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Big_is_beautiful.jpg/500px-Big_is_beautiful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Big_is_beautiful.jpg/1280px-Big_is_beautiful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Big_is_beautiful.jpg/500px-Big_is_beautiful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stuffed toy rabbit in Burkina Faso","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABig_is_beautiful.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG/500px-Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG/1280px-Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG/500px-Comercio_de_peluches_en_Lima%2C_Per%C3%BA%2C_2015-07-28%2C_DD_47.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai